  "findings": [
    {
      "finding": "The defect is architectural, not a property of C03. S1_tip_first, the earliest strategy study, already builds the leading edge with 2 to 4 wrap cells, and S6_bounded_mesh_atlas inherited that construction. Every level in every family carries it: coarse, smoke, medium, fine, C01, C02 and C03.",
      "id": "C1",
      "severity": "CRITICAL"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Refinement does not relieve it. Across the families the wrap moves only from 3 to 5 points while chordwise and spanwise counts roughly double, so turning per cell improves from about 38 to about 25 degrees and never approaches the target. A grid-convergence study on any of these families would therefore not be in the asymptotic range for pressure-derived quantities.",
      "id": "C2",
      "severity": "HIGH"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Nothing in the existing gate set detects this. Integrated forces, residual convergence, y+, cell quality, inversion counts and interface conformity all pass on these meshes. The defect is visible only in the surface pressure at the nose or in the mesh geometry itself.",
      "id": "C3",
      "severity": "HIGH"
    }
  ],
